# Title:  New Windows service installed
# MITRE:  T1543.003 - Create or Modify System Process: Windows Service
# Data:   System channel, EventCode 7045 (classic WinEventLog, not XML)
# Why:    Services run as SYSTEM and start automatically, which makes service creation a
#         favourite persistence and privilege-escalation route. PsExec and most lateral
#         movement tooling leaves a 7045 behind.
# Noise:  Legitimate software installs create services. Volume is low enough on a
#         workstation to review each one, which is the right posture for this detection.
# NOTE:   Field names beyond EventCode are unverified -- the Security/System channels use
#         classic rendering and Splunk_TA_windows extraction, which has not been confirmed
#         on this instance yet. EventCode itself is always present.

index=endpoint source="WinEventLog:System" EventCode=7045
| table _time, host, Service_Name, Service_File_Name, Service_Type, Service_Start_Type
| sort - _time
